# brev/nv-models.list: the NVIDIA Inference Hub models a Brev box's pi offers (J499). brev/nv-models.mjs turns it into provider
# "nv-inference" in the box's ~/.pi/agent/models.json, reading the box's own key (~/workspace/.secrets/nv_inference_key).
# One model per line:  id  api  contextWindow  maxTokens  [default]
#   api: completions (Claude, Gemini, open models) or responses (OpenAI GPT); "default" marks pi's default model and Thoughts'.
# To add a model, add one line (ids: GET https://inference-api.nvidia.com/v1/models with the key). Run `world X setup` again.
azure/anthropic/claude-opus-5-5      completions  200000   32000   default
azure/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5    completions  200000   32000
azure/anthropic/claude-haiku-4-5     completions  200000   32000
openai/openai/gpt-6.1-sol            responses    1050000  128000
gcp/google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview    completions  1048576  65536
# Not yet chosen (uncomment to add):
# openai/openai/gpt-6-sol            responses    1050000  128000
# openai/openai/gpt-6-astra          responses    1050000  128000
